[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Stubbing Methods with when() and thenReturn() in Mockito"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"Stubbing is the process of defining canned answers (return values) for method calls on mock objects during unit testing. In Mockito, this is primarily achieved using the combination of Mockito.when() and the thenReturn() method."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"Prerequisites and Setup"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"Before using when() and thenReturn(), ensure you have properly imported Mockito static methods in your test class to keep your code clean and readable."},{"order":5,"type":"code","text":"import static org.mockito.Mockito.when;
import static org.mockito.Mockito.mock;
import static org.junit.jupiter.api.Assertions.assertEquals;
import org.junit.jupiter.api.Test;"},{"order":6,"type":"subheading","text":"Basic Stubbing Example"},{"order":7,"type":"paragraph","text":"Consider a scenario where you have a UserService dependency that fetches user roles from a database. Since you are unit testing the dependent service, you want to mock the database call."},{"order":8,"type":"code","text":"public interface DatabaseService {
    String getUserRole(String userId);
}"},{"order":9,"type":"paragraph","text":"To stub this method, you create a mock of the DatabaseService interface and define its behavior using when()."},{"order":10,"type":"code","text":"@Test
public void testGetAdminRole() {
    // 1. Create the mock object
    DatabaseService databaseMock = mock(DatabaseService.class);

    // 2. Stub the method using when() and thenReturn()
    when(databaseMock.getUserRole("user123")).thenReturn("ADMIN");

    // 3. Execute and verify
    String role = databaseMock.getUserRole("user123");
    assertEquals("ADMIN", role);
}"},{"order":11,"type":"subheading","text":"Stubbing Multiple Consecutive Calls"},{"order":12,"type":"paragraph","text":"You can configure a mock method to return different values on consecutive calls by passing multiple arguments to thenReturn()."},{"order":13,"type":"code","text":"@Test
public void testConsecutiveCalls() {
    DatabaseService databaseMock = mock(DatabaseService.class);

    when(databaseMock.getUserRole("user123"))
        .thenReturn("GUEST")
        .thenReturn("USER")
        .thenReturn("ADMIN");

    assertEquals("GUEST", databaseMock.getUserRole("user123"));
    assertEquals("USER", databaseMock.getUserRole("user123"));
    assertEquals("ADMIN", databaseMock.getUserRole("user123")); // subsequent calls will also return ADMIN
}"},{"order":14,"type":"subheading","text":"Best Practices"},{"order":15,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Only stub methods that return values (avoid using when() on void methods; use doNothing() instead)."},{"order":16,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Keep stubbing logic close to the test setup to maintain high readability."},{"order":17,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Avoid over-stubbing unneeded methods, as it can make tests brittle."}]
